"}, "language": "english", "review": "When I saw Astartes on YouTube I thought, \"Oh man, this looks like the awesomest ♥♥♥♥ ever.\"\n\nThose videos make Space Marines feel heavy, precise, and absolutely lethal.. every movement looks deliberate, every fight feels tense and controlled.\n\nThis game is not that.\n\nEven at a discount, it just wasn't fun for me. The Warhammer 40K universe is still cool, but the gameplay completely misses what made Astartes so good. Instead of tactical, weighty combat, it turns into pretty brainless hack & slash. You just mash through enemies without much thought, and it gets repetitive fast.\n\nThe environments and style are decent, but there is no real depth to the gameplay to back it up. It never gave me that feeling of being a disciplined, unstoppable Space Marine.. just a generic action character in a 40K skin.\n\nMaybe that works for some people, but it didn't for me. I refunded it.", "timestamp_created": 1775592636, "timestamp_updated": 1775592977, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.476190477609634399", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1725898212", "reactions": []}]}